  "generated_text": ".. **Identify the dimensions of the pyramid:**\n   - The height of the pyramid is 12 inches.\n   - The base of the pyramid is a square with each side measuring 10 inches.\n\n2. **Determine the smallest cube-shaped box that can contain the pyramid:**\n   - The of of the cube must be at least the height of the pyramid, which is 12 inches.\n   - The side length of the cube must be at least the side length of the base of the pyramid, which is 10 inches.\n\n3. **Calculate the volume of the cube:**\n   - The volume \\( V \\) of a cube is given by the formula \\( V = s^3 \\), where \\( s \\) is the side length of the cube.\n   - Here, \\( s = 12 \\) inches (since the height of the cube must be at least 12 inches).\n   - Therefore, the volume \\( V \\) is \\( V = 12^3 = 1728 \\) cubic inches.\n\n4. **::**\n   - The volume of the smallest cube-shaped box to contain the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{1728}\\) cubic inches.",
  "grade": {
